# Empower Jace puts its counters only on a Jace planeswalker TOKEN (the card's ruling: "empower Jace won't let you put
# loyalty counters on nontoken Jace planeswalkers"), so with Jace, the Mind Sculptor (a card, 3 loyalty) already under Bot1's
# control it makes its own token and the Mind Sculptor stays at 3. Before that, a second Sanctum beholds the Mind Sculptor
# on the battlefield: a permanent, so it is chosen and nothing is revealed, and the land enters untapped. The first Sanctum
# entered tapped on turn 1 (Bot1 declined to behold the Mind Sculptor from its hand).

[Bot1 Deck]
Theorist's Sanctum
Theorist's Sanctum
Black Lotus
Jace, the Mind Sculptor
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Island
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Theorist's Sanctum.Play
Bot1.Choose()
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Jace, the Mind Sculptor.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Jace, the Mind Sculptor.Counters.Loyalty = 3
Bot1.Hand.Theorist's Sanctum.Play
Bot1.Choose(Jace, the Mind Sculptor)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Theorist's Sanctum#2.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Theorist's Sanctum#1.Activate(Ability: Empower)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Theorist's Sanctum#2.Activate
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Jace, the Mind Sculptor.Counters.Loyalty = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Jace Token.Counters.Loyalty = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Jace Token.Token = true
Bot1.Revealed = (absent)
